# WARP-8: a kit's Steps page is a grid of its eleven keys (pages.c kit_grid): a black key picks the lane, the white
# keys write its steps, and the other lanes' steps stay as they are; the layout audit passes with every lane named
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
tap SEQ
expect page Steps
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w8
expect note 1 1 1 1
expect note 1 1 9 1
tapkey b1
tapkey w4
tapkey w8
expect note 1 1 5 2
# (a kit step's note: its first sound; step 9 has the kick and the snare, then the snare alone)
expect note 1 1 9 1
tapkey b0
tapkey w8
expect note 1 1 9 2
shot kitgrid.png
tap PLAY
wait 600
shot kitgrid_playing.png
tap PLAY
